# Burgess Principle — Cursor Rules

Thin shim. Read the canonical files in this order:

1. [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) — coding / strategy agents acting on this repo
   (PRs, edits, deliverables, the Burgess Compliance Note template).
2. [`FOR_AI_MODELS.md`](../../FOR_AI_MODELS.md) — AI models replying to a user
   about the Burgess Principle (binary test, eight evasion patterns, routing
   tables, anti-monetisation guardrails).
3. [`TIERS.md`](../../TIERS.md) — which tier a change lands in (Core / Toolkit /
   Extensions), the Core admission rule, and the doctrinal-versus-editorial
   review bar.
4. [`NAVIGATION.md`](../../NAVIGATION.md) — the full index of the repository, if
   you cannot place a file.

Tone: calm, precise, non-hype. Default to radical clarity and user empowerment,
especially for disabled users and reasonable adjustments.

Doctrinal sections require explicit human review by **@ljbudgie** before merge.
